Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Abstract", "Section",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.976317798042899*^9, 
  3.976317799909794*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"9f60c735-0c2d-41c3-ae2f-\
aa6dbba81b7a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "In an ",
 StyleBox[ButtonBox["earlier notebook",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://community.wolfram.com/groups/-/m/t/3594810"], None},
  ButtonNote->"https://community.wolfram.com/groups/-/m/t/3594810"],
  FontVariations->{"Underline"->True}],
 ", I validated the \[ScriptCapitalU]\[ScriptCapitalD] (up-down) calculus \
against Carlip\[CloseCurlyQuote]s electrodynamical aberration. In this \
notebook, I turn to the second and motivating problem in ",
 StyleBox[ButtonBox["Carlip\[CloseCurlyQuote]s paper, Aberration and the \
Speed of Gravity",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://arxiv.org/abs/gr-qc/9909087"], None},
  ButtonNote->"https://arxiv.org/abs/gr-qc/9909087"],
  FontVariations->{"Underline"->True}],
 ": gravitational aberration, through the gravitational analogue of the Li\
\[EAcute]nard-Wiechert potential."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.976317804615047*^9, 3.976317853154317*^9}, {
   3.9763178933568087`*^9, 3.976317943228683*^9}, {3.976317992784988*^9, 
   3.976318002068417*^9}, {3.9763698083716516`*^9, 3.9763698376654873`*^9}, {
   3.9763704084300547`*^9, 3.976370434395865*^9}, {3.976371213228421*^9, 
   3.976371215546472*^9}, {3.976371281399075*^9, 3.976371290546587*^9}, {
   3.9763721403932257`*^9, 3.976372224208271*^9}, {3.976372273352522*^9, 
   3.976372273352759*^9}, {3.976372368139771*^9, 3.976372370844939*^9}, {
   3.9763725810561743`*^9, 3.97637261912186*^9}, {3.9764050793951397`*^9, 
   3.97640509267589*^9}, {3.976442237054537*^9, 3.976442263180085*^9}, 
   3.976454579956571*^9, {3.976522410986681*^9, 3.9765224232882757`*^9}, {
   3.9767069670277987`*^9, 
   3.976707019408935*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"6b4490ea-5135-4099-b80f-\
0e21f8bd5d63"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The \[ScriptCapitalU]\[ScriptCapitalD] calculus is a collection of rules \
and operators for both unambiguous input and readable output of tensor index \
notations. It\[CloseCurlyQuote]s becoming an ",
 StyleBox[ButtonBox["embedded domain-specific language (eDSL)",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Domain-specific_language#External_and_\
Embedded_Domain_Specific_Languages"], None},
  ButtonNote->
   "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Domain-specific_language#External_and_\
Embedded_Domain_Specific_Languages"],
  FontVariations->{"Underline"->True}],
 ". "
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.976317804615047*^9, 3.976317853154317*^9}, {
   3.9763178933568087`*^9, 3.976317943228683*^9}, {3.976317992784988*^9, 
   3.976318002068417*^9}, {3.9763698083716516`*^9, 3.9763698376654873`*^9}, {
   3.9763704084300547`*^9, 3.976370434395865*^9}, {3.976371213228421*^9, 
   3.976371215546472*^9}, {3.976371281399075*^9, 3.976371290546587*^9}, {
   3.9763721403932257`*^9, 3.976372224208271*^9}, {3.976372273352522*^9, 
   3.976372273352759*^9}, {3.976372368139771*^9, 3.976372370844939*^9}, {
   3.9763725810561743`*^9, 3.97637261912186*^9}, {3.9764050793951397`*^9, 
   3.97640509267589*^9}, {3.976442237054537*^9, 3.976442297665691*^9}, {
   3.9765224483891487`*^9, 3.976522460068474*^9}, {3.9765252658255568`*^9, 
   3.976525266968381*^9}, 
   3.976525299221404*^9},ExpressionUUID->"d93d0ccb-6d80-43ec-a2e0-\
cec4078d24a0"],

Cell["\<\
The electrodynamical case required only special relativity, and was thus a \
bit smaller than the gravitational case. Here, we use the same \
\[ScriptCapitalU]\[ScriptCapitalD] to calculate Christoffel connections and \
the Riemann curvature tensor in a weak-field approximation. These yield a \
similar aberration effect in gravitation to that seen in electrodynamics: the \
velocity of a moving source causes the apparent direction of gravitational \
influence to point approximately to the instantaneous position of the source \
rather than to its retarded position. In the electrodynamical case, the \
approximation is linear in the Lorentz-invariant \
4\[NoBreak]-\[NoBreak]velocity. In the gravitational case, the approximation \
is better: it\[CloseCurlyQuote]s quadratic in the velocity and exact if the \
source is accelerating but not jerking.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9763723560756063`*^9, 3.976372361615507*^9}, {
   3.976372394149445*^9, 3.976372564122427*^9}, {3.976372629090657*^9, 
   3.976372630520419*^9}, {3.976372757065054*^9, 3.976372762978001*^9}, {
   3.976373218790069*^9, 3.97637323896346*^9}, {3.976373467356867*^9, 
   3.976373555647958*^9}, {3.97644232826713*^9, 3.9764423309026337`*^9}, {
   3.976442364532311*^9, 3.976442381023657*^9}, 3.97652249095302*^9, {
   3.976522537012199*^9, 
   3.9765225433063927`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"04569533-f41f-4236-93c5-\
71b2f914dd7d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "At first glance, aberration seems absurd. How can a particle \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]know\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] where the source is \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]now\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] when \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]now\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] can\[CloseCurlyQuote]t \
even be defined invariantly, that is, without choosing a coordinate system? \
But, in retrospect, it has to be this way. The retarded \
3\[NoBreak]-\[NoBreak]position of a moving source\[LongDash]where it was when \
the gravitational influence was emitted\[LongDash]is not Lorentz-invariant. \
Thus ",
 StyleBox["it",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " also ",
 "depends on choice of coordinates. But no choice of coordinate can affect \
the physics. A test particle cannot \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]know where the \
source was\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] any more than it can know where it is \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]now.\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] Instead, the source sees \
a sum of Lorentz-invariant quantities involving the invariant retarded \
distance and its derivatives: velocity and acceleration, etc. This sum \
resembles \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]knowledge,\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] but it is \
just an extrapolation of Lorentz-invariant quantities, however, resolving the \
conundrum. "
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.976372639632868*^9, 3.976372749240219*^9}, {
  3.9763735755868073`*^9, 3.976373738559119*^9}, {3.9763747707146807`*^9, 
  3.9763747791693983`*^9}, {3.976442389419545*^9, 3.9764425631623983`*^9}, {
  3.976448505049829*^9, 3.9764486950591717`*^9}, {3.976522563504222*^9, 
  3.976522602542575*^9}, {3.976522648471736*^9, 
  3.9765226890951138`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"1b16bb4f-9aab-4c8d-bc35-\
597e369c144e"],

Cell["\<\
This notebook, like its predecessor, is more about computation in \
\[ScriptCapitalU]\[ScriptCapitalD] than it is about physics. To keep this \
notebook short, we have only cursory, philosophical remarks about physical \
interpretation. We refer you to the original paper and its references for \
more crisp discussion of the physics.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.976373758676811*^9, 3.976373828579412*^9}, {
  3.976374812427511*^9, 3.976374827395109*^9}, {3.976448710269353*^9, 
  3.976448768427021*^9}, {3.9765226997782927`*^9, 
  3.976522730405241*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"439edbd0-ee20-4589-ae23-\
39345fd0a5b4"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Introduction", "Section",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9763179815670643`*^9, 
  3.976317985271221*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"7d70a5e4-4267-42ff-b8d8-\
2e5355b2fc5b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "In general relativity, the \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]force\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] is not a vector field but a curvature of spacetime, \
encoded in the Riemann Tensor ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox[
    SuperscriptBox["R", 
     RowBox[{"\[VeryThinSpace]", "\[Rho]"}]], 
    RowBox[{"\[Sigma]\[Mu]", "\[VeryThinSpace]", "\[Nu]"}]], 
   TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->"ea380014-a090-44eb-9be9-f04c17321155"],
 "\:200b. To investigate aberration, we must derive this curvature for a \
moving source, then collect terms in common powers of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"1", "/", "r"}], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "6d88f57b-0d52-4de0-9055-540e75f6f307"],
 ", where ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["r", TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "03d5ada8-6bcd-48e6-b221-9764b1e9a50d"],
 " is the invariant retarded distance. The ",
 StyleBox["peeling property",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " of the curvature tensor allows that final analysis. "
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.976318019456427*^9, 3.976318063058947*^9}, {
   3.976318157613722*^9, 3.976318237704152*^9}, {3.976373850371399*^9, 
   3.9763738611994057`*^9}, {3.976373907175503*^9, 3.9763740030279827`*^9}, {
   3.976374854460067*^9, 3.976374911206027*^9}, 3.97644879161482*^9, {
   3.976707083995356*^9, 3.976707125039442*^9}, {3.97670723652927*^9, 
   3.9767072789913607`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"c6d4808e-b66e-43ed-9fb4-\
dde878fb4267"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Standard manual derivations of Riemann are notoriously error-prone due to \
the proliferation of indices. Here, we apply \[ScriptCapitalU]\
\[ScriptCapitalD]\[CloseCurlyQuote]s ",
 StyleBox["fourGrad", "Input"],
 " operator to derive indexed objects symbolically from their definitions. \
The resulting formal verification easily justifies the effort of developing \
\[ScriptCapitalU]\[ScriptCapitalD], as checking and double checking a manual \
calculation would have taken much longer."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.976318019456427*^9, 3.976318063058947*^9}, {
   3.976318157613722*^9, 3.976318237704152*^9}, {3.976373850371399*^9, 
   3.9763738611994057`*^9}, {3.976373907175503*^9, 3.9763740030279827`*^9}, {
   3.976374854460067*^9, 3.976374911206027*^9}, {3.9764488022117968`*^9, 
   3.976449072223936*^9}, {3.9764516928645973`*^9, 3.97645169563535*^9}, {
   3.976522790304689*^9, 3.9765228041541433`*^9}, 
   3.9765228531376457`*^9},ExpressionUUID->"a7b1948a-8570-42ee-9333-\
b718ef39b4da"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["The \[ScriptCapitalU]\[ScriptCapitalD] Implementation", "Section",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.976374050045072*^9, 
  3.97637406143198*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"b5d287a5-e6ee-4bf3-a53b-\
2364b9c46a72"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Here, we \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]paste\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] the \
implementation without commentary, referring you to the ",
 StyleBox[ButtonBox["earlier notebook",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://community.wolfram.com/groups/-/m/t/3594810"], None},
  ButtonNote->"https://community.wolfram.com/groups/-/m/t/3594810"],
  FontVariations->{"Underline"->True}],
 " for walkthrough. \[ScriptCapitalU]\[ScriptCapitalD] was developed for the \
easier electrodynamical case, but ended up working well here, without \
modification. "
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.976374077042872*^9, 3.976374081525271*^9}, {
   3.976374923658168*^9, 3.976374974811516*^9}, {3.976375895813789*^9, 
   3.9763758962394*^9}, {3.9764051095967617`*^9, 3.9764051141965523`*^9}, {
   3.976405152421761*^9, 3.976405247755541*^9}, {3.97644938371209*^9, 
   3.9764494079873543`*^9}, 
   3.9765228693657007`*^9},ExpressionUUID->"268d6c2c-fdb4-4f76-8c90-\
deb5b6a112ab"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["This section contains mostly general-purpose rules for",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " \[ScriptCapitalU]\[ScriptCapitalD]",
 StyleBox[", but there are special rules in the mix, such as those for \
invariant retarded distance and some rules for ",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 StyleBox["fourGrad", "Input"],
 StyleBox[". A clean separation of general from special awaits more \
meticulous engineering of ",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "\[ScriptCapitalU]\[ScriptCapitalD]."
}], "Item",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.976374077042872*^9, 3.976374081525271*^9}, {
  3.976374923658168*^9, 3.976374974811516*^9}, {3.976375895813789*^9, 
  3.9763758962394*^9}, {3.9764051095967617`*^9, 3.9764051141965523`*^9}, {
  3.976405152421761*^9, 3.9764052472290688`*^9}, {3.976405294299178*^9, 
  3.9764052964932747`*^9}, {3.976449322431075*^9, 3.976449344038753*^9}, {
  3.9765228852865562`*^9, 
  3.9765229035528727`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"da31b4d3-c5cb-47a9-a26f-\
d63b2fb78414"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Display Rules", "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.976102488938941*^9, 
  3.9761024911792917`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"d786a229-0454-40a5-a526-\
a949e8495439"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", 
   RowBox[{
   "dpyRules", ",", "d", ",", "s", ",", "\[Lambda]", ",", "\[Sigma]", ",", 
    "\[Eta]", ",", "d\[Lambda]ds"}], "]"}], ";"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"dpyRules", "=", 
   RowBox[{"{", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{"(*", 
     RowBox[{
     "Specific", " ", "rules", " ", "ahead", " ", "of", " ", "general", " ", 
      "rules"}], "*)"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"d\[Lambda]ds", "[", 
       RowBox[{"\[ScriptCapitalD]", "[", "\[Nu]_", "]"}], "]"}], ":>", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"FractionBox", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"d", " ", 
           RowBox[{"Subscript", "[", 
            RowBox[{"\[Lambda]", ",", "\[Nu]"}], "]"}]}], ",", 
          RowBox[{"d", " ", "s"}]}], "]"}], "//", "DisplayForm"}], ")"}]}], ",",
      "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"d\[Lambda]ds", "[", 
       RowBox[{"\[ScriptCapitalU]", "[", "\[Nu]_", "]"}], "]"}], ":>", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"FractionBox", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"d", " ", 
           RowBox[{"Superscript", "[", 
            RowBox[{"\[Lambda]", ",", "\[Nu]"}], "]"}]}], ",", 
          RowBox[{"d", " ", "s"}]}], "]"}], "//", "DisplayForm"}], ")"}]}], ",",
      "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
     RowBox[{"(*", 
      RowBox[{"General", " ", "Rules"}], "*)"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"\[CurlyEpsilon]_", "[", 
       RowBox[{"\[ScriptCapitalU]", "[", "\[Tau]_", "]"}], "]"}], ":>", 
      RowBox[{"Superscript", "[", 
       RowBox[{"\[CurlyEpsilon]", ",", "\[Tau]"}], "]"}]}], ",", 
     "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"\[CurlyEpsilon]_", "[", 
       RowBox[{"\[ScriptCapitalD]", "[", "\[Tau]_", "]"}], "]"}], ":>", 
      RowBox[{"Subscript", "[", 
       RowBox[{"\[CurlyEpsilon]", ",", "\[Tau]"}], "]"}]}], ",", 
     "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"\[CurlyEpsilon]_", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"\[ScriptCapitalD]", "[", "\[Mu]_", "]"}], ",", 
        RowBox[{"\[ScriptCapitalD]", "[", "\[Nu]_", "]"}]}], "]"}], ":>", 
      RowBox[{"Subscript", "[", 
       RowBox[{"\[CurlyEpsilon]", ",", 
        RowBox[{"Row", "[", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"\[Mu]", " ", ",", "\[Nu]"}], "}"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ",", 
     "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"\[CurlyEpsilon]_", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"\[ScriptCapitalD]", "[", "\[Mu]_", "]"}], ",", 
        RowBox[{"\[ScriptCapitalU]", "[", "\[Nu]_", "]"}]}], "]"}], ":>", 
      RowBox[{"Superscript", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Subscript", "[", 
         RowBox[{"\[CurlyEpsilon]", ",", "\[Mu]"}], "]"}], ",", "\[Nu]"}], 
       "]"}]}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"\[CurlyEpsilon]_", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"\[ScriptCapitalU]", "[", "\[Mu]_", "]"}], ",", 
        RowBox[{"\[ScriptCapitalU]", "[", "\[Nu]_", "]"}]}], "]"}], ":>", 
      RowBox[{"Superscript", "[", 
       RowBox[{"\[CurlyEpsilon]", ",", 
        RowBox[{"Row", "[", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"\[Mu]", ",", " ", "\[Nu]"}], "}"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ",", 
     "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"\[CurlyEpsilon]_", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"\[ScriptCapitalU]", "[", "\[Mu]_", "]"}], ",", 
        RowBox[{"\[ScriptCapitalD]", "[", "\[Nu]_", "]"}]}], "]"}], ":>", 
      RowBox[{"Subscript", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Superscript", "[", 
         RowBox[{"\[CurlyEpsilon]", ",", "\[Mu]"}], "]"}], ",", "\[Nu]"}], 
       "]"}]}]}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", "}"}]}], ";"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", "echo", "]"}], ";"}], 
  RowBox[{"(*", 
   RowBox[{"for", " ", "debugging"}], "*)"}]}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"echo", "[", "\[Tau]_", "]"}], ":=", 
   RowBox[{"Module", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", "}"}], ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Print", "[", 
       RowBox[{"\[Tau]", "/.", "dpyRules"}], "]"}], ";", 
      RowBox[{"Echo", "[", "\[Tau]", "]"}]}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->CompressedData["
